WEBVTT

00:43.626 --> 00:48.631
DOONA!

00:50.925 --> 00:52.010
"I'm glad."

00:53.595 --> 00:54.929
That's what she said?

00:57.348 --> 00:58.683
That she was glad?

00:58.725 --> 00:59.809
EPISODE 3
SPRING BREEZE

00:59.893 --> 01:03.438
Yeah. What do you think that means,
from a girl's point of view?

01:03.521 --> 01:04.606
Mmm…

01:05.148 --> 01:07.442
Well, I think it could mean two things.

01:09.694 --> 01:10.695
Number one,

01:11.946 --> 01:13.990
"I'm glad nothing's going on,

01:14.074 --> 01:16.284
'cause I plan on keeping you
all to myself."

01:16.367 --> 01:17.702
"I like you, Won-jun."

01:19.579 --> 01:21.206
Number two, "Doona?"

01:21.706 --> 01:24.459
"Mmm. I'm not really a fan of Doona's."

01:25.210 --> 01:27.087
"Well, good thing
you're not seeing her then."

01:28.338 --> 01:29.714
Or it's neither of those two.

01:30.924 --> 01:32.759
Hey, are you stupid?

01:32.842 --> 01:34.094
Of course it's number one

01:34.677 --> 01:36.638
Why would a girl like Jin-ju
like me, you know?

01:39.474 --> 01:40.850
Why wouldn't she like you?

01:41.392 --> 01:42.811
Because I'm a fan.

01:45.438 --> 01:47.023
What's with the smile on your face, huh?

01:48.817 --> 01:51.820
It's not that, um,
don't think I'm a great guy,

01:51.903 --> 01:55.281
but we've known each other
for a while, and I don't want to ruin it.

01:57.492 --> 01:59.577
I think that you
might be overthinking it.

02:00.912 --> 02:02.330
Just live in the present, huh?

02:03.164 --> 02:06.126
Hey, it's not like Jin-ju is a…
a mind reader, you know?

02:06.209 --> 02:07.377
I'm definitely not.

02:08.378 --> 02:11.131
In the chance, you end up getting hurt,
you can cry on my shoulder, hmm?

02:11.214 --> 02:13.508
That's what real friends are for, huh?

02:30.567 --> 02:31.484
Hmm.

02:36.364 --> 02:37.866
THE ART OF MATHEMATICS

02:41.077 --> 02:43.621
FOR SOPHOMORES
THE ART OF MATHEMATICS

03:00.763 --> 03:03.892
Oh! Won-jun, Won-jun, come quick.

03:03.975 --> 03:04.809
- Okay.
- Close that.

03:04.893 --> 03:05.810
All right.

03:05.894 --> 03:08.688
Five. Four. Three.

03:08.771 --> 03:10.899
Two. One.

03:14.736 --> 03:17.363
Five. Four. Three.

03:17.947 --> 03:19.490
Two. One.

03:22.410 --> 03:24.162
- Okay, what's next?
- Five.

03:24.245 --> 03:26.122
- Four. Three.
- Finger hearts, Won-jun.

03:26.206 --> 03:28.041
Two. One.

03:29.918 --> 03:31.085
What are you doing?

03:31.669 --> 03:33.213
Hold on. Do it right.

03:33.296 --> 03:36.090
- Like this. There you go.
- Five.

03:36.174 --> 03:40.011
Four. Three. Two. One.

03:54.234 --> 03:57.904
There's a rumor
that you and I might be together.

03:57.987 --> 03:59.239
Uh-huh, I heard.

03:59.322 --> 04:00.198
But it's not true,

04:00.782 --> 04:02.450
'cause we're just friends, right?

04:02.533 --> 04:06.621
Uh, what do you tell everyone
whenever they ask you

04:06.704 --> 04:08.331
what the deal is between us?

04:09.040 --> 04:09.916
You go first.

04:10.875 --> 04:12.085
What do you tell people?

04:12.168 --> 04:14.837
Well… so…

04:15.922 --> 04:17.257
I just say that we're close.

04:19.050 --> 04:20.343
That we get along well.

04:23.304 --> 04:24.973
Like soulmates kind of.

04:30.645 --> 04:31.646
Oh, really?

04:32.438 --> 04:34.524
I like that. Soulmates, huh?

04:47.662 --> 04:49.664
Mmm, this one came out good.

04:50.748 --> 04:52.125
Only you look good.

04:52.750 --> 04:55.503
No, you look good in it too!

06:04.072 --> 06:06.532
Happy birthday. I'll be in touch.

07:36.956 --> 07:39.083
Here you go.
Apologies for the wait.

07:39.167 --> 07:41.127
We have a lot of drink orders
at the moment.

07:41.210 --> 07:42.128
Please enjoy.

08:06.777 --> 08:09.113
I'm so sorry.
I spilled some coffee over there.

08:09.197 --> 08:11.532
Ah, okay. Um, I… Well, I can get it.

08:11.616 --> 08:13.951
Oh. Thank you, Won-jun.

08:25.880 --> 08:26.964
Jin-ju?

08:28.549 --> 08:29.634
Hmm?

08:30.218 --> 08:31.969
Do you have any plans tomorrow?

08:32.762 --> 08:33.763
Uh…

08:34.847 --> 08:37.475
Well, the cherry blossoms are out.
But you probably can't go.

08:37.558 --> 08:38.684
No, wait, uh…

08:41.812 --> 08:42.813
Okay.

08:44.565 --> 08:45.566
Okay, great, then.

09:42.957 --> 09:44.625
Doona, where are you?

09:47.753 --> 09:48.921
Hey, Doona, are you there?

09:52.508 --> 09:53.884
Is that you knocking? Doona!

09:58.931 --> 10:00.558
Doona!

10:03.769 --> 10:05.605
Doona, are you…
are you in there?

10:06.105 --> 10:07.189
I can't get out.

10:09.150 --> 10:10.276
Can you break down the door?

10:10.359 --> 10:12.111
Just hang on
for a little longer.

11:22.431 --> 11:24.058
What are you thinking about right now?

11:27.228 --> 11:28.145
You're so sexy.

11:29.313 --> 11:32.358
A man who fixes bathroom doors,
it's so sexy and cool.

11:32.441 --> 11:34.944
Ah, you're so incorrigible, you know that?

11:37.405 --> 11:38.531
No, seriously.

11:39.740 --> 11:41.325
It's probably from not having a father.

11:42.243 --> 11:44.995
So this kind of thing
has always been a fantasy of mine.

11:45.746 --> 11:47.373
Ah, so, um, is he not around?

11:48.040 --> 11:48.874
Mm-mm.

11:48.958 --> 11:50.793
I also lost my father when I was young.

11:55.131 --> 11:56.674
I never had one to begin with.

11:58.008 --> 12:00.219
I guess life must've been
really hard for you too, then.

12:00.302 --> 12:01.429
It wasn't.

12:03.055 --> 12:03.973
Believe it or not,

12:04.640 --> 12:06.559
I found it really convenient.

12:06.642 --> 12:08.602
I could imagine my father
to be anyone I'd like.

12:10.479 --> 12:12.231
But do you know what's really hard?

12:13.023 --> 12:15.192
It's not the people
who were never there to begin with.

12:15.776 --> 12:18.571
But it's when you lose the people
that were always there from the start.

12:19.071 --> 12:21.407
That's enough to drive you really insane.

12:25.995 --> 12:26.996
Look at that.

12:27.079 --> 12:28.831
Of course these disappeared too.

12:31.417 --> 12:32.710
Oh, I, uh…

12:32.793 --> 12:36.046
I saw some cigarettes in your cabinet
when I was looking for the tools.

12:37.715 --> 12:38.549
Oh, those?

12:51.729 --> 12:52.980
These aren't mine.

12:55.149 --> 12:57.401
I would never smoke crappy cigarettes.

12:58.319 --> 12:59.403
Hey, Doona.

13:00.488 --> 13:02.323
Uh, should we go outside?

13:04.074 --> 13:05.910
Instead of smashing bottles
over people's heads,

13:05.993 --> 13:07.912
this is a better alternative.
Just give it a shot.

13:09.789 --> 13:10.873
Grab hold of the hammer.

13:11.832 --> 13:12.666
Like this.

13:20.716 --> 13:23.344
Faster!

13:23.427 --> 13:26.764
You gotta whack hard to score. Think
of everything you hate, then smash it.

13:26.847 --> 13:30.434
Faster!
Hee-hee-hee! Getting angry?

13:34.146 --> 13:35.689
There's a pattern, you see? Take a look.

13:36.190 --> 13:38.317
That hurts! That hurts! That hurts!

13:38.400 --> 13:40.611
- Don't hit me! Don't hit me!
- You're doing great!

13:40.694 --> 13:43.364
That hurts! That hurts!

13:43.447 --> 13:44.782
It's fun, right?

13:44.865 --> 13:46.033
Oh, there's one!

13:46.116 --> 13:47.993
Here. Here. There.

13:48.077 --> 13:50.412
That hurts!

13:50.496 --> 13:52.248
- Great job!
- Whoa!

13:52.331 --> 13:53.290
You did good.

13:53.374 --> 13:55.376
- I wanna go again.
- Hmm.

13:55.960 --> 13:57.336
Go for it.

13:57.419 --> 13:59.338
That hurts! That hurts!

13:59.421 --> 14:01.799
That's it.

14:01.882 --> 14:04.301
Don't hit me!

14:04.385 --> 14:05.553
That hurts!

14:05.636 --> 14:07.221
YOUR SCORE

14:13.686 --> 14:14.895
That hurts!

14:24.280 --> 14:26.198
- Boo! Boo!
- How did I miss that?

14:30.369 --> 14:31.495
Hey! Oh!

14:32.705 --> 14:33.789
Oh!

14:38.002 --> 14:40.421
- Get in there!
- Whoo!

14:43.924 --> 14:45.718
Give it to me! Give it to me!

14:47.803 --> 14:48.804
Ah!

14:50.514 --> 14:51.682
Wanna play some more?

15:05.529 --> 15:06.488
Go ahead.

15:10.784 --> 15:12.661
I'm beat.

15:17.583 --> 15:18.417
Hey.

15:20.252 --> 15:21.670
You should lie on your back.

15:23.714 --> 15:25.341
It's really pretty. Look.

15:39.188 --> 15:40.689
Why are you laughing?

15:41.482 --> 15:43.567
Well, it's just…
What are you calling pretty?

15:43.651 --> 15:44.777
I can't see a single star.

15:45.361 --> 15:47.196
It's completely overcast right now.

15:48.572 --> 15:51.742
- It's probably gonna rain tonight.
- Do you think so?

15:55.162 --> 15:56.497
It's a beautiful sky.

15:57.790 --> 15:59.041
I don't care if it rains.

16:05.547 --> 16:07.716
Thank you for everything, Won-Jun.

16:08.759 --> 16:10.094
It was so much fun.

16:10.678 --> 16:11.637
I had fun too.

16:12.513 --> 16:15.975
I can't remember the last time
I let go and had so much fun like this.

16:22.272 --> 16:24.525
I asked Jin-ju to come with me
and see the cherry blossoms.

16:27.111 --> 16:28.862
Really? She said yes?

16:29.822 --> 16:31.657
Uh… oh, uh, well, I…

16:31.740 --> 16:33.367
I kind of thought she'd say no, but yeah.

16:33.450 --> 16:35.536
To be honest,
I was surprised she said yes.

16:37.287 --> 16:40.165
Don't run away from her.
You can't keep doing that, okay?

16:42.835 --> 16:44.169
Okay, I… I won't.

17:22.458 --> 17:23.584
Hmm.

17:24.626 --> 17:25.461
Hmm.

17:25.961 --> 17:28.130
Mmm, the weather is…

17:28.213 --> 17:29.339
SEOUL WEATHER CLEAR

17:29.423 --> 17:30.507
…clear and sunny.

17:53.322 --> 17:54.656
- Won-jun!
- Oh. Oh.

17:55.324 --> 17:57.826
Let's go.

17:59.244 --> 18:01.747
Oh, they're so pretty!

18:01.830 --> 18:04.625
They are, aren't they?
There's so many cherry blossoms falling.

18:04.708 --> 18:05.876
Mm-hmm.

18:05.959 --> 18:07.002
Oh, right, hey.

18:07.086 --> 18:11.381
Kook Su-jin's apartment complex
has gorgeous cherry blossoms, remember?

18:11.465 --> 18:12.633
Ah, I definitely remember.

18:12.716 --> 18:14.218
That's when we skipped a day of school

18:14.301 --> 18:16.220
and went
to the playground in front of his place.

18:18.180 --> 18:20.307
What? We didn't skip a whole day.

18:20.390 --> 18:22.309
You were scared to miss class,

18:22.392 --> 18:24.853
so we went back after 20 minutes
so they wouldn't count you out.

18:26.772 --> 18:32.027
Lee Won-jun wouldn't ever arrive late
for a class, let alone skip, hmm?

18:32.611 --> 18:33.904
You're really something else.

18:36.782 --> 18:38.075
Wow.

18:38.158 --> 18:39.368
Wow.

18:44.581 --> 18:46.125
- Hey, the other day--
- There was some--

18:46.208 --> 18:47.793
You go ahead. Please, be my guest.

18:47.876 --> 18:49.837
No, you go first.

18:50.963 --> 18:53.465
Uh, so the other day, I found this game,

18:53.549 --> 18:55.884
the one you liked to play
when we were back in high school.

18:55.968 --> 18:57.427
Seriously?

18:57.511 --> 18:59.513
Oh, I totally miss playing that.

18:59.596 --> 19:02.349
I haven't played it here in Seoul.
So did you play it?

19:02.850 --> 19:05.310
Uh, actually, no. Doona was playing it.

19:05.811 --> 19:07.104
She never played it before.

19:07.187 --> 19:09.231
Well, everything is a first for her.

19:10.482 --> 19:11.483
Hmm.

19:13.652 --> 19:15.654
Um, what were you going to say earlier?

19:15.737 --> 19:16.738
Well, um,

19:18.323 --> 19:19.658
I forgot already. Hmm.

19:24.496 --> 19:25.330
Oh.

19:27.583 --> 19:30.169
- It's starting to rain.
- Ah.

19:32.754 --> 19:33.589
Ah.

19:58.280 --> 19:59.114
Hey, Jin-ju!

20:00.866 --> 20:01.992
Se-hun?

20:07.831 --> 20:10.417
A towel. Where is it?

20:11.835 --> 20:13.921
- Oh, here.
- Oh, thanks, man.

20:14.004 --> 20:15.631
Here, put this over you.
You're pretty wet.

20:15.714 --> 20:16.757
Oh, thanks.

20:25.682 --> 20:26.516
YUN-TAEK

20:26.600 --> 20:28.435
Is it all right
if I take this call right now?

20:28.518 --> 20:29.561
Oh, please do. No worries.

20:31.230 --> 20:32.606
Hey, Yun-taek.

20:32.689 --> 20:34.900
Won-jun, when are you back?
We got pizza.

20:34.983 --> 20:36.735
It was two for one, so we got four.

20:36.818 --> 20:38.278
- Uh…
- I know that voice.

20:38.362 --> 20:41.198
Hey, are you talking
to Seo Yun-taek by chance?

20:41.281 --> 20:44.034
Uh, yes. How did you know it was Yun-taek?

20:44.117 --> 20:47.621
Wow, it really is
such a small world.

20:47.704 --> 20:49.831
Who would've guessed
Won-jun's friend from back home

20:49.915 --> 20:53.377
and my best friend
would, uh, connect like this?

20:53.460 --> 20:55.295
Amazing, right?

20:55.379 --> 20:59.549
Jin-ju, what can I say about Se-hun?
I may be biased because he's my friend,

20:59.633 --> 21:02.386
but that's one impressive bastard there,
for real. I'm serious.

21:02.469 --> 21:04.179
- First of all, he's tall.
- You're too kind.

21:04.263 --> 21:06.765
He's good-looking. Oh… and wealthy.

21:06.848 --> 21:09.643
And don't forget,
he's freaking amazing at sports,

21:09.726 --> 21:11.520
which is why his body is amazing.

21:11.603 --> 21:13.105
You look at his legs, whoa!

21:13.188 --> 21:16.400
- You lucked out for sure, Jin-ju. No joke!
- Hey, don't be that guy.

21:16.483 --> 21:18.443
He's always like this when he's drunk.
Ignore him.

21:18.527 --> 21:20.320
It's totally fine.

21:23.031 --> 21:25.909
Anyways, so are
the two of you dating or what?

21:26.576 --> 21:28.078
Uh, I wouldn't say that. We're just--

21:28.161 --> 21:30.247
I'd say
we're more like soulmates.

21:30.330 --> 21:32.207
We get along so well, it's special.

21:32.874 --> 21:33.959
Uh-huh.

21:34.042 --> 21:35.127
Oh!

21:35.210 --> 21:39.006
Then you should be dating.
You have to date now.

21:39.089 --> 21:40.757
You should kiss her!

21:40.841 --> 21:43.260
- Oh! Huh?
- Hey, Yun-taek. Eat the food.

21:43.343 --> 21:44.219
Here.

21:44.303 --> 21:46.555
Because if you keep speaking,
you'll die of starvation.

21:46.638 --> 21:48.724
Oh, wow. Really?

21:49.349 --> 21:51.435
You finally acknowledged me
by my name just now.

21:51.518 --> 21:53.312
Does that mean
you know I actually exist?

21:53.395 --> 21:55.856
- Oh, this is amazing!
- Man, you really need a tranquilizer.

21:55.939 --> 21:58.734
- You seriously talk too much.
- Am I talking too much?

21:59.234 --> 22:00.652
You can talk too, you know?

22:00.736 --> 22:03.655
Besides, you can't rain on this parade,
because Dream Sweet knows who I am!

22:03.739 --> 22:05.532
Doona, I'll go get
some ice cream for everyone.

22:06.241 --> 22:07.075
Okay.

22:07.159 --> 22:09.244
Let's celebrate! Woo-hoo!

22:09.745 --> 22:11.663
Cheers!

22:11.747 --> 22:14.791
You see, this guy over here,
when we did our national service…

22:42.861 --> 22:43.987
Oh, you're here,

22:44.071 --> 22:46.031
my soulmate.

22:53.330 --> 22:55.999
It looks like I have to retake my exams.

22:57.667 --> 23:01.046
I wanted us to go to university together,
but now it won't happen.

23:01.880 --> 23:02.714
Mmm.

23:04.341 --> 23:06.259
Wow, it's getting really cold.

23:34.496 --> 23:36.164
Is that a little better now?

23:43.046 --> 23:43.964
Not really.

23:45.507 --> 23:47.342
I still feel so cold, Won-jun.

24:11.366 --> 24:12.367
Hmm?

24:17.289 --> 24:19.124
Your taste is similar to a grandma's.

24:19.624 --> 24:21.418
For example,
like the toe socks you're wearing.

24:22.502 --> 24:23.795
Aren't you cold at all?

24:23.879 --> 24:26.006
Hmm. Don't worry. I'm immune to the cold.

24:29.885 --> 24:30.719
Whoa.

24:33.305 --> 24:35.849
- These cherry blossoms are different.
- What is it?

24:36.475 --> 24:37.809
Look at the petals.

24:37.893 --> 24:40.937
Yangjin and Seoul's are different
from each other, but so are these ones.

24:44.566 --> 24:46.109
Well, should I tell you why that is?

24:46.651 --> 24:47.611
Do you know?

24:49.362 --> 24:51.031
Those weren't cherry blossoms at all, huh?

24:51.114 --> 24:53.492
Those were actually peach blossoms,
you dummy.

24:53.575 --> 24:56.328
Oh. Where did you learn that?

24:56.828 --> 24:58.747
I guess
I'm just smarter than you, Mr. Lee.

24:59.247 --> 25:01.625
You should address me
as your teacher from now on.

25:01.708 --> 25:02.667
Yes, Teacher.

25:03.251 --> 25:04.503
You go ahead, okay?

25:05.587 --> 25:07.631
- What are you doing?
- I'm gonna smoke.

25:08.715 --> 25:10.258
Uh, I can stay with you if you want.

25:10.342 --> 25:13.261
Mm-mm. The ice cream will melt otherwise.

25:14.179 --> 25:16.014
- Throw this away, will you?
- Yep.

25:17.516 --> 25:18.391
All right, then.

25:34.741 --> 25:37.827
- Here we are. Ice cream.
- Whoa, ice cream.

25:39.120 --> 25:40.038
Thanks a lot.

25:40.664 --> 25:41.748
There you go.

25:42.749 --> 25:45.460
- Here you go. It's your favorite.
- Oh, thank you so much.

25:45.961 --> 25:48.046
- Hey, Won--
- Doona, get your ice cream!

25:49.839 --> 25:51.466
What were you talking about?

25:51.550 --> 25:53.009
Huh? Oh, yeah, yeah.

25:53.093 --> 25:54.386
All right, so,

25:55.220 --> 25:57.264
the wild boar is charging right at me.

25:57.764 --> 25:59.683
And they're really fast, you know?

26:00.183 --> 26:02.519
I obviously couldn't outrun it.
I knew it immediately.

26:02.602 --> 26:04.479
So I thought, "I'll jump on its back!"

26:05.522 --> 26:07.482
I went for it and landed on its back.

26:07.983 --> 26:09.818
But I was turned around!

26:09.901 --> 26:12.571
So I'm on backwards,
and this thing never even slows down.

26:12.654 --> 26:14.906
People are shouting,
"Hey, where are you going?"

26:14.990 --> 26:17.450
"I'll return on boar-back. Don't worry!"

26:17.534 --> 26:19.452
So then I grabbed its tail,
you know, to steer.

26:19.536 --> 26:22.330
- Come on. Stop lying.
- Of course it's a lie, jackass.

26:22.414 --> 26:24.874
How could it possibly be true?
Seriously, dude.

26:24.958 --> 26:26.835
You're so drunk.

26:27.335 --> 26:30.255
- So, just flirting right now?
- So far, yes, just flirting.

26:30.338 --> 26:31.506
Mmm.

26:31.590 --> 26:32.966
Jin-ju's really cute, right?

26:33.550 --> 26:34.384
Huh?

26:37.470 --> 26:38.805
Hell yeah.

26:39.431 --> 26:41.391
Anyway, congratulations, man.

26:49.274 --> 26:50.942
Doona, can we hang out again sometime?

26:53.111 --> 26:54.237
Whenever you'd like.

27:01.953 --> 27:03.288
Over here!

27:05.498 --> 27:07.417
Let's go, literature team!

27:07.500 --> 27:09.085
Pass it! Block them!

27:16.718 --> 27:18.720
Come on! Whoo!

27:18.803 --> 27:21.056
- They're gonna end up fighting.
- There's no way.

27:21.139 --> 27:23.600
Won-jun would never do that.
He'd give up the ball in that case.

27:26.353 --> 27:28.229
- Go! Go get him!
- All right!

27:28.897 --> 27:29.981
Come on!

27:31.775 --> 27:33.693
Whoo!

27:33.777 --> 27:36.780
Yes, Se-hun! Whoo!

27:36.863 --> 27:37.906
You got this.

27:40.283 --> 27:41.451
KOR LIT
CIV ENG

27:41.534 --> 27:43.036
- Oh.
- Yeah.

27:43.745 --> 27:45.455
Hey, Jin-ju, could you
hold onto this for me?

27:46.039 --> 27:47.582
Oh, sure. Uh…

27:47.666 --> 27:49.292
Go, literature team!

27:49.918 --> 27:52.504
- Come on, Se-hun. Go get him!
- Hey, Jeong!

27:54.547 --> 27:56.091
There it goes! There it goes!

27:56.174 --> 27:57.342
Block it!

27:59.844 --> 28:02.138
Whoo!

28:02.222 --> 28:03.473
Whoo!

28:03.556 --> 28:05.642
- Whoo!
- Yay.

28:08.144 --> 28:09.062
Whoo!

28:12.482 --> 28:14.317
- Take care of that leg.
- Good job, everyone.

28:14.943 --> 28:15.860
All right.

28:18.571 --> 28:20.323
- Good work, guys!
- Thanks.

28:23.201 --> 28:25.078
Jin-ju, are you coming with me
to lunch today?

28:25.161 --> 28:26.538
Oh, actually…

28:26.621 --> 28:28.373
There's a new pasta place
across the street.

28:29.207 --> 28:30.750
- Let's go together.
- Uh…

28:31.918 --> 28:34.170
I should head back to school
because I still have class.

28:34.254 --> 28:35.338
Oh.

28:35.422 --> 28:36.673
How about just us?

28:38.508 --> 28:40.218
Mm-hmm. All right.

28:40.301 --> 28:41.970
- Let's play again, okay?
- All right.

28:45.098 --> 28:46.057
Well, I'll get going.

28:46.683 --> 28:47.517
Let's eat, hmm?

28:52.981 --> 28:54.733
So is this new pasta place good?

29:08.538 --> 29:10.498
Did you miss class because of me?

29:10.582 --> 29:12.125
I didn't wanna go anyway.

29:15.336 --> 29:16.880
You let that boy take her away.

29:17.464 --> 29:18.840
You could lose her for good.

29:18.923 --> 29:20.800
Listen, Miss Teacher,
how could I lose her, hmm?

29:20.884 --> 29:22.010
She isn't mine to lose, okay?

29:22.093 --> 29:23.678
What are you saying?

29:23.762 --> 29:25.054
'Cause from what I see,

29:25.138 --> 29:27.307
you and Jin-ju
definitely have feelings for one another,

29:27.390 --> 29:29.225
but you guys aren't doing anything.

29:29.309 --> 29:31.394
At least tell her how you feel
before you give up.

29:31.478 --> 29:33.188
Just watching you both
just makes me get mad.

29:34.898 --> 29:35.940
I did try already.

29:36.941 --> 29:39.152
I told her I had feelings for her
a long time ago.

29:39.235 --> 29:40.278
She knew how I felt.

29:42.322 --> 29:43.156
She did?

29:43.740 --> 29:44.908
Yeah.

29:44.991 --> 29:47.243
At the time, I thought
she had feelings too.

29:57.337 --> 29:58.338
I really like you.

30:18.233 --> 30:20.527
Sorry, the number
you're trying to reach…

30:20.610 --> 30:22.237
Is everything okay?

30:25.490 --> 30:26.574
Sorry.

30:26.658 --> 30:29.160
I've just been super busy.
I'll talk to you later.

30:33.915 --> 30:34.833
MAYBE

30:36.668 --> 30:39.963
COULD WE

30:46.427 --> 30:50.265
COULD YOU COME OUT FOR

30:52.559 --> 30:55.687
- This could feed two dozen people.
- We can definitely finish this.

30:55.770 --> 30:58.106
- Of course we can eat it.
- Of course we can!

30:59.023 --> 31:00.775
Let's do it!

31:10.034 --> 31:11.035
Okay.

31:14.330 --> 31:15.373
Take care.

31:25.049 --> 31:26.134
We lost touch after that,

31:26.217 --> 31:28.720
and we didn't see each other
for over a year.

31:33.016 --> 31:34.350
It was my fault, really.

31:36.185 --> 31:37.228
What was?

31:37.312 --> 31:40.398
Well, making assumptions
about someone else's feelings towards you.

31:41.608 --> 31:44.360
And overstepping the mark
without any real conviction to do so.

31:45.028 --> 31:45.904
'Cause of that,

31:46.779 --> 31:48.948
at that time,
it cost me a very good friend.

31:52.452 --> 31:54.746
But luckily, it's water under the bridge.

31:54.829 --> 31:58.374
And now I'm just really happy that we
can be friends once again, you know?

32:00.335 --> 32:01.419
So I'm grateful.

32:05.214 --> 32:08.217
So in that case, um,
your teachings can officially stop.

32:10.553 --> 32:12.805
Wow,
I can't believe I just got fired.

32:13.431 --> 32:14.265
What a bummer.

32:14.349 --> 32:16.434
And I never got paid for my services.

32:23.816 --> 32:24.901
SE-HUN

32:28.321 --> 32:30.907
Uh… I'll be right back, okay?

32:55.974 --> 32:57.183
Who's there?

33:23.876 --> 33:25.878
Doona really must be getting
super bored, huh?

33:25.962 --> 33:27.797
She always wants to hang out with you.

33:27.880 --> 33:31.467
She never had friends until now.
I feel a little sorry for her.

33:32.927 --> 33:35.596
She really seems
to rely on you a lot lately.

33:36.180 --> 33:39.308
Nah, she just likes to make fun of me.
I'm not much to rely on.

33:40.101 --> 33:42.311
- Should we get some chips?
- Mm-hmm.

33:49.193 --> 33:51.529
You should give yourself
a little more credit, Won-jun.

33:53.531 --> 33:54.991
You're totally reliable.

33:57.118 --> 33:59.495
Sorry for the wait.
I'll check you out now.

34:00.997 --> 34:03.166
Oh, that's right.
It's April Fools' Day.

34:04.375 --> 34:06.711
So did you all, um, tell some lies today?

34:06.794 --> 34:09.338
Let's hear 'em all now.
What have you guys got?

34:10.506 --> 34:11.340
I love you.

34:12.467 --> 34:13.676
Like a lot.

34:14.218 --> 34:15.511
Oh, I love you too.

34:16.012 --> 34:18.347
- You jerk, I should kick you in the face!
- Ah! Calm down!

34:19.390 --> 34:21.100
Someone told me today he liked me.

34:26.439 --> 34:28.191
I still haven't responded to him.

34:28.816 --> 34:29.650
Why not?

34:31.944 --> 34:34.072
'Cause I'm not sure how I feel about him.

34:38.284 --> 34:39.368
It's really weird.

34:40.286 --> 34:42.789
When there's someone
that I'm into a whole lot,

34:44.207 --> 34:46.834
as soon as they approach me,
I totally lose my nerve.

34:48.211 --> 34:50.671
I worry they'll be disappointed somehow.

34:52.673 --> 34:54.842
Especially when they learn who I am.

35:04.352 --> 35:06.020
What's wrong?

35:07.105 --> 35:08.689
Weren't we supposed to lie?

35:08.773 --> 35:10.566
Jeez, you guys!

35:10.650 --> 35:12.819
Seriously, you should see your faces.

35:12.902 --> 35:15.196
Huh? I'm so impressed by your acting.

35:15.279 --> 35:18.491
Is that like method acting?
Just now, I was totally absorbed by her.

35:18.574 --> 35:21.536
Ugh, Doona's not a good influence.
You should stop hanging out with her.

35:21.619 --> 35:24.539
I thought that was awesome, Jin-ju.
Good job, huh?

35:25.957 --> 35:27.917
So next is, um, Miss Doona.

35:29.168 --> 35:32.505
What's your lie, Doona? It's gonna be hard
to follow Jin-ju's act, right?

35:32.588 --> 35:35.049
I'm being stalked by a guy,
and I don't know who he is.

35:36.425 --> 35:39.887
- What a weird concept for a lie.
- Believe me. I wish it were a lie.

35:44.016 --> 35:45.351
YOU'RE PRETTY

35:46.435 --> 35:47.311
It isn't.

35:47.395 --> 35:48.396
Doona, what is this?

35:51.732 --> 35:52.859
You're so pretty.

35:54.527 --> 35:55.486
He's among us now.

36:02.201 --> 36:05.204
What the hell?
Whoa! Who the hell was that?

36:05.788 --> 36:06.873
Oh, wait. What?

36:07.415 --> 36:08.374
You creep!

36:14.797 --> 36:16.215
Hey you! Stop!

36:16.299 --> 36:17.717
- Hey!
- Won-jun!

36:18.384 --> 36:19.302
Hey!

36:19.385 --> 36:21.012
Stop that punk! You bastard!

36:21.846 --> 36:23.973
Get him! That… Ugh!

36:24.056 --> 36:25.558
- Get him!
- He turned that way!

36:28.144 --> 36:30.146
- Oh! Oh!
- I've got it! Ah!

36:30.229 --> 36:32.273
- Are you all right?
- I've got his bag. Yes, thanks.

36:32.940 --> 36:34.650
- Are you okay?
- Oh, we got it.

36:34.734 --> 36:37.028
We need to get used to this.
There's gonna be more stalkers.

36:43.201 --> 36:44.410
Hey, let go of me!

36:45.745 --> 36:47.914
You're busted! I got you!

36:47.997 --> 36:49.832
Ah! Let go!

36:51.584 --> 36:53.628
Hey! There he is! You bastard!

36:54.295 --> 36:56.130
Son of a bitch!

36:56.214 --> 36:58.841
- Won-jun, are you okay?
- Who do you think you are?

36:59.759 --> 37:01.844
Hey, help me get a hold of this creep!

37:01.928 --> 37:04.138
Hold him. Hold him. Hold him.
How dare you?

37:23.532 --> 37:24.742
This isn't good.

37:26.035 --> 37:26.953
- What is it?
- What?

37:28.537 --> 37:30.456
He's seriously a little shit.

37:31.082 --> 37:34.919
I just did it out of pure curiosity.
I swear that's what it was!

37:35.002 --> 37:37.171
She came into the convenient store
and I got excited.

37:37.255 --> 37:38.631
I worship her, guys, truly!

37:44.762 --> 37:46.347
We should handle this ourselves.

37:46.430 --> 37:47.932
Exactly what do you have in mind?

37:48.015 --> 37:49.934
We should beat his ass.
That's what he deserves.

37:51.519 --> 37:52.979
I'll do it here and now.

37:54.730 --> 37:56.732
I'll do it until he's
on the verge of being dead.

37:58.651 --> 38:02.446
Maybe I'll go for his head first.
I bet that would feel really good.

38:09.495 --> 38:11.205
I've always wanted
to smash someone's head.

38:11.289 --> 38:12.456
- No!
- Wait, Doona.

38:12.540 --> 38:14.458
Whoa!

38:30.433 --> 38:33.185
Oh, wow. She didn't do it.

38:33.269 --> 38:35.354
Oh, thank goodness,
someone's thinking rationally.

38:37.440 --> 38:38.274
- Ah!
- Listen.

38:39.150 --> 38:41.319
I'll kill you if you say one more word,
you got it?

38:41.902 --> 38:42.945
I'm truly sorry.

38:56.751 --> 38:59.462
Do you really think
it's all right not to call the police?

39:00.713 --> 39:02.298
Doona is dead set against it.

39:03.424 --> 39:04.800
She must have her reasons.

39:06.093 --> 39:09.263
Are you all right?
You look like you're hurt pretty ba--

39:09.347 --> 39:10.473
Really, it's okay.

39:17.438 --> 39:20.066
So, it looks like
I'm gonna be leaving home soon.

39:20.149 --> 39:21.609
That's why I'm working so much.

39:22.485 --> 39:25.237
My dad was always against it,
but I'm moving.

39:26.030 --> 39:27.990
I did wonder what was going on.

39:28.699 --> 39:29.575
Really?

39:58.187 --> 39:59.021
DAD

39:59.105 --> 40:00.940
WHY AREN'T YOU BACK HOME YET, YOU BITCH?

40:01.023 --> 40:03.901
YOU THINK I SENT YOU TO COLLEGE
SO YOU CAN FOOL AROUND WITH MEN?

40:03.984 --> 40:04.985
TEXT ME BACK RIGHT NOW

40:05.069 --> 40:05.903
I'M ON MY WAY

41:26.650 --> 41:28.277
YOU'VE GOTTEN BETTER AT LYING

41:28.360 --> 41:30.863
STOP CONTACTING ME AND WAIT QUIETLY

42:02.394 --> 42:03.562
Won-jun, you're here.

42:05.397 --> 42:07.650
- Yeah, hey.
- Why are you down here?

42:07.733 --> 42:09.652
Oh, I couldn't sleep at all.

42:10.736 --> 42:12.238
Can I have one of your beers?

42:22.581 --> 42:24.333
Why don't you sit down for a second?

42:42.977 --> 42:45.062
We got a copy
of the stalker's identification,

42:45.145 --> 42:46.313
the memory card,

42:46.397 --> 42:48.941
even a written statement
promising to never do it again.

42:49.441 --> 42:51.235
We got everything
that we thought you'd need.

42:51.318 --> 42:53.612
We also went to his home
and wiped out both of his computers

42:53.696 --> 42:55.197
of any pictures or videos,

42:55.281 --> 42:57.032
and he also agreed to quit his job.

42:57.992 --> 43:00.703
We told his parents and the store manager
what happened as well.

43:03.038 --> 43:06.000
So now, I'll give you everything, and, uh,

43:07.459 --> 43:10.588
well, when you feel ready to present this
at the police, you can at your own time.

43:10.671 --> 43:11.672
It's your choice.

43:12.381 --> 43:13.299
Okay, thanks.

43:16.260 --> 43:17.678
I appreciate your help.

43:21.599 --> 43:24.643
So, um, it must've been scary
having to deal with that alone.

43:26.770 --> 43:27.605
It wasn't.

43:33.569 --> 43:34.570
Hey, Doona.

43:36.864 --> 43:40.826
It's okay to be scared, you know?
It's a lot better than you getting hurt.

43:45.039 --> 43:47.416
Actually,
I never wanna see you get hurt ever.

43:48.000 --> 43:50.294
What I hope for you
is to be loved by everyone again.

44:06.477 --> 44:08.187
I think I'm ready to go to bed now.

44:09.188 --> 44:10.314
I need to sleep.

44:43.514 --> 44:45.474
Do you mind if we hold hands?

44:47.476 --> 44:49.937
If you don't like it,
you can pull your hand away.
